1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,803
Parking bays and amenities can now charge
by the day or

2
00:00:03,803 --> 00:00:07,606
by the month, and every fee goes straight
into the books.

3
00:00:07,606 --> 00:00:11,409
Open the property, then its Parking tab,
and edit bay B2-18.

4
00:00:11,409 --> 00:00:13,829
Set the fee type to Per month,

5
00:00:13,829 --> 00:00:16,249
and the amount to five hundred dirhams.

6
00:00:16,249 --> 00:00:17,978
The income account is optional.

7
00:00:17,978 --> 00:00:21,781
Left empty, parking fees go to the
property's Additional Parking account.

8
00:00:21,781 --> 00:00:22,126
Save.

9
00:00:22,126 --> 00:00:24,892
The office can also book for a tenant.

10
00:00:24,892 --> 00:00:26,621
In Bookings, select New booking.

11
00:00:26,621 --> 00:00:29,732
Choose the property and the unit, and the
tenant

12
00:00:29,732 --> 00:00:32,498
on its live contract fills in by itself.

13
00:00:32,498 --> 00:00:35,610
Choose Parking, bay B2-18, from today for
one month.

14
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:38,375
The fee is worked out before you book:

15
00:00:38,375 --> 00:00:41,141
five hundred dirhams, plus VAT where it
applies.

16
00:00:41,141 --> 00:00:42,524
Select Book and approve.

17
00:00:42,524 --> 00:00:45,290
The booking is approved at once, and the

18
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:47,710
fee is posted as a journal voucher.

19
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:50,476
Rent Receivable for Ahmed is debited five
hundred,

20
00:00:50,476 --> 00:00:53,241
and Additional Parking income is credited
five hundred.

21
00:00:53,241 --> 00:00:56,007
The narration names the bay and the dates.

22
00:00:56,007 --> 00:00:59,810
On Ahmed's contract, a row now collects
the five hundred, like

23
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:03,267
any other payment, and he sees it in his
payments.

24
00:01:03,267 --> 00:01:03,959
Plans change.

25
00:01:03,959 --> 00:01:06,725
Ahmed hands the bay back the same day.

26
00:01:06,725 --> 00:01:08,799
Open the booking and select Release.

27
00:01:08,799 --> 00:01:12,602
Today counts as used; the rest of the
month is credited.

28
00:01:12,602 --> 00:01:16,059
A second voucher takes four hundred and
eighty-three dirhams, thirty-three

29
00:01:16,059 --> 00:01:19,171
back out of parking income, and the row
Ahmed

30
00:01:19,171 --> 00:01:22,282
still has to pay drops to sixteen dirhams,
sixty-seven.

31
00:01:22,282 --> 00:01:25,048
A booking that has not started yet is

32
00:01:25,048 --> 00:01:27,814
cancelled instead, and its whole fee is
reversed.

33
00:01:27,814 --> 00:01:30,234
Tenants see the fee before they ask.

34
00:01:30,234 --> 00:01:32,654
In the tenant portal, Fatima opens
Facilities.

35
00:01:32,654 --> 00:01:35,420
The Fitness Centre costs thirty dirhams a
day.

36
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:37,840
She picks a date, and the fee

37
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:40,260
is shown before she submits: thirty
dirhams.

38
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:44,063
When the office approves, the fee is
charged to her contract

39
00:01:44,063 --> 00:01:47,520
in the same way, and she is told the
amount.
